# ZOOM-BOUNCE-2: hammer both zoom limits with notches that arrive within a few
# frames of each other (some with no wait at all between pushes), at the owner's
# own cursor position and window size, looking for a one-frame presented-scale
# overshoot at or just past a limit (leads 1 and 2 of the review). Run with
# (needs the original game files and a GPU):
#   python -I tools/test/viewer_wiring.py <exe> zoom_bounce_2 <out dir> --gpu --trace
#     --env ANNO_VIEW_SIZE=2560x1369 --app-arg --play --app-arg data/maps/lan5.txt
#     --app-arg --construction-menu --app-arg on --app-arg --water --app-arg enhanced
# then check <out dir>.trace/frames.tsv (scale vs resample_scale, and the
# resample-scale-derived eased tile width) for a one-frame disagreement. The REPORTS
# evidence run used 40 repeats here; regenerate a longer version with the same shape
# from a copy of this file's own generator (see the REPORTS entry).
look 1080 635
wait ms 1500
# repeat 0: closest limit
wheel -12 1080 635
wait ms 20
wheel -12 1080 635
wait ms 20
wheel -12 1080 635
wait ms 20
